// An assignment's target decides which node it becomes: a bare name is an
// assign, `obj.name` a set, `arr[0]` a set-index, `*p` a set-deref. The
// compound operator is carried on the node rather than desugared away.
yo x = 1
yo arr = [1, 2]
yo obj = {"name": 0}
yo p = &x
x = 1
obj.name = 1
arr[0] = 1
x += 1
*p = 1
*p += 1
// `&` binds at unary precedence, so it takes the postfix chain and stops.
yo cmp = &arr[0] == &arr[1]
// `&&` wins maximal munch; an address-of after it needs the space.
yo both = x && &x
